# api's build context became the repo root (see docker-compose.yaml's
# api.build - needed to COPY lj-controller/ into the image). Without this
# file, `docker build` would upload the whole repo - including .git
# history and any local runtime data - to the daemon on every build.
.git
.gitignore
data/
# Docker's .dockerignore matching is NOT recursive by default the way
# .gitignore's is - a bare `__pycache__/` only matches at the context
# root, not nested under e.g. lj-controller/ or api/app/. Needs the `**/`
# prefix to match at any depth (confirmed: without it, a stray local
# lj-controller/__pycache__/ still got copied into the image).
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
lj-controller/config.yaml
